From 95c29f0d744856307bb6fbcc237fd4cfb5b700b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Slava P." <slavap@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:45:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rdna-boosts [optional]: two-lane prefill
 (LLAMA_PREFILL_LANES) -- consecutive-ubatch overlap

From PR #268 by @slavap, rebased onto the current delivery set (r220) and reduced to
what the delivery does not already carry:

- DROPPED: `cpy_tensor_async_nowait` and its CUDA implementation, and the per-copy
  event ring.  r220 folded those into the delivery (block 12) from this same PR, so
  the optional patch now USES `ggml_backend_sched_next_copy_event` /
  `cpy_tensor_async_nowait` instead of defining them.
- DROPPED: the second copy of `ggml_backend_sched_next_copy_event`.
- FIXED: the event code no longer spells `hipEventDefault` / `hipEventElapsedTime`
  unconditionally (`ggml-cuda.cu` still builds for CUDA via nvcc): the elapsed-time
  hook uses `cudaEventElapsedTime`, and the backend's events are created with
  timing ONLY when `GGML_SCHED_PAIR_DEBUG>=3`, the one consumer of elapsed time, so
  applying this patch costs the default path nothing.
- FIXED: the documented `-sm layer -ts 1,1` dense layout is refused by the feature's
  own gate on this tree; the README states which layouts are reachable and why.

LLAMA_PREFILL_LANES=2 builds two consecutive prefill ubatches on a second backend
scheduler and submits their splits alternately
(ggml_backend_sched_graph_compute_async_pair), so one device's routed experts overlap
the other device's attention on a wide prefill.  Opt-in, default 1 (single lane); it
degrades to the existing path when < 2 non-CPU backends, pipeline parallelism,
no_alloc, or a draft context (ctx_other) is present, and a ubatch is paired only when
it is wide, output-free, and no nextn (MTP) or F1 layer-input readback is active.

Reachability on this delivery (measured, 3x R9700 / gfx1201): `-sm tensor` counts ONE
backend (the Meta device wrapping N GPUs) so the pair never engages; plain `-sm layer`
enables the scheduler's own pipeline parallelism and the feature declines.  The
reachable layouts are ones that already disable pipeline parallelism, i.e. with
`--override-tensor`, which is the layout this patch was measured in.

Measured here with the pair engaged (pair decided: splits a=4 b=4, interleaved=1):
MoE 35B-A3B Q8_0 pp8192 +0.03 %, dense 27B Q6_K_XL nil -- i.e. throughput-neutral on
balanced devices.  The submitter's +34 % / +13 % are on a 7900 XTX + V620 pair, where
the two devices differ ~3x and the overlap hides the imbalance.

Validated here: greedy text byte-identical between lanes (prompts/prose-rdna-boosts.txt,
-n 64, --temp 0 --seed 42); no abort with MTP; default path unchanged.
